<title>UK: UK shortlists 3 to buy social security property.</title>
<headline>UK shortlists 3 to buy social security property.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Social Security said on Friday it had narrowed the list of potential bidders for the privatisation of its property estate to three.</p>
<p>They are:</p>
<p>-- Partnership Property Management Ltd, a consortium including Goldman Sachs International.</p>
<p>-- Mapely Holdings Ltd, which includes NationsBank.</p>
<p>-- OPUS, which includes Nomura International Plc.</p>
<p>Social Security Secretary Peter Lilley said in a written parliamentary answer that the three consortia would be invited to submit detailed bids that would be evaluated in early 1997.</p>
<p>The property sale is expected to raise between two billion and four billion stg, according to press reports.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
